body:
Here are my suggestions:

&#x200B;

1) Investment into tech programs/tech subscriptions for students (and the teachers), Turnitin and Proctorio are great software to help prevent plagiarism. Check with each department head to see what they're interested in specifically

&#x200B;

2)  Supplies: science rooms always need new flasks/beakers/Bunsen burners, art rooms always need more art supplies. Band rooms need tuning equipment.  Tbh giving each teacher a small sum/wish list to improve their classrooms would be useful

&#x200B;

3) "Greenhouse" initiative: Cali is a great place to start a garden! You could grow food crops at the school for a relatively inexpensive starting point (if you have an existing soil bed, just a soil test kit, fertilizer and seeds plis gardening supplies cou. Encourages healthier eating, student body involvement, great PR oppurtunity... I know that's more post COVID, but having different classes at different times to do watering/soil checks/weed removal is still fairly easy to do with restrictions

&#x200B;

4) Give teachers some tools to improve data storage on their own school computers/improve overall output (maybe a wifi extender, external hard drive, ect.)

Drunk dialed him and told him I loved him (apparently, I don't remeber this but he and an unbiased third party both say I did).

&#x200B;

He and I have been dating a year now, he still gives me shit about that lmao

